{"name":"Homoeopathic Red","hex":"#ecdbe0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"homoeopathic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of homeopathic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homoeopathic"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Homeopathy","blocks":[{"text":"Homeopathy or homoeopathy is a pseudoscientific system of alternative medicine. It was conceived in 1796 by the German physician Samuel Hahnemann. Its practitioners, called homeopaths or homeopathic physicians, believe that a substance that causes symptoms of a disease in healthy people can cure similar symptoms in sick people; this doctrine is called similia similibus curentur, or \"like cures like\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg/330px-Saxonia_Museum_fuer_saechsische_Vaterlandskunde_III_19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeopathy","wikidata":"Q81058"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/1280px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Homeopathy-2.jpg/500px-Homeopathy-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeopathy-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/1280px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg/500px-Samuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Samuel Hahnemann Monument, Washington, D.C., with the inscription Similia Similibus Curentur – \"Like cures Like\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASamuel_Hahnemann_Monument%2C_Scott_Circle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/H